{{#if (eq elixirApi "grpc")}}
## gRPC

The application starts the generated Greeter service on `127.0.0.1:50051`. Set `GRPC_PORT` to
choose another port. Production releases bind the service to all interfaces. The protobuf contract
is `priv/protos/greeter.proto`; its message definitions and client stub are included under
`lib/{{elixirAppName}}/grpc/`.

From the running application's IEx session:

```elixir
{:ok, channel} = GRPC.Stub.connect("127.0.0.1:50051", connect_timeout: 2_000)
request = %{{elixirModuleName}}.Rpc.HelloRequest{name: "Better Fullstack"}
{:ok, reply} = {{elixirModuleName}}.Rpc.Greeter.Stub.say_hello(channel, request, timeout: 2_000)
reply.message
GRPC.Stub.disconnect(channel)
```

`say_hello` returns `invalid_argument` for an empty name or a name longer than 80 characters.
`mix test` exercises the real server and client on a temporary local port, including that error.

After changing the protobuf contract, regenerate its definitions with `protoc` and the Elixir
protobuf plugin, then update the server implementation:

```sh
protoc --elixir_out=plugins=grpc:lib/{{elixirAppName}}/grpc -I priv/protos priv/protos/greeter.proto
```
{{/if}}
